			<div class="content" id="post-content-1509942">
									

<p>Kalinin , Kalinin, why do you do this.<br />
First, you somewhat creep me out with the first picture, enough that I thought it was some noob that's trying to pass with it by.<br />
Then, i read, and my little feline heart gets all happy and want to upvote it hard.<br />
Then come the documents, and well.. the first one is stupid for several reasons, while the last is a nice addition, but not much punch after what's been said already, at least in my opinion.</p>
<p>As for the memo, it's far too general to be of any interest - that this is challenging, everyone has figured, and there aren't too many things that couldn't be stated by one sentence in the containment procedures (such as recommended cover story)</p>
<p>Then, you get this.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The recent development of amnestic drugs for use in information control has provided the Foundation with a very useful tool. However, due to questions about lingering aftereffects on brain chemistry and the potential impact on governmental figures, the use of these drugs in containing information about SCP-1377 is prohibited without my express consent.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Which is both unbelievable (we consider worse things than that acceptable) and hell.. his express content? I'd get that if he was an O5, but then he wouldn't be reviewing it either because O5 are busy - they'd likely set up a committee.</p>
<p>I can't upvote it with clear conscience as it is, but fuck, do I love the description and the footage.<br />
This article is like watching porn, and just as the chick undresses and starts playing with her boobs, the video switches to two frogs mating.</p>

							</div>

								
					
